28/08/2026

Problem : Integrating external railway data with Smart-Cross
The project depended on railway data from an external source, but the application needed that 
information in a format suitable for its own calculations.

Solution: We used a separate railway data integration layer to retrieve the available train 
information and pass it to the backend's crossing-timing logic.



4/09/2026

Problem : Testing the application without live railway data
Depending entirely on a live railway API made development and testing difficult whenever the
external data source was unavailable.

Solution: We added a mock-data option controlled by configuration. This enabled us to test the 
backend's processing and the frontend's display using sample railway data.


7/09/2026

Problem : Managing delays and repeated API requests
Repeatedly requesting train information can increase response time and place unnecessary load
on an external API. Railway data also may not need to be fetched again for every user request.

Solution: We included a configurable cache duration so that recently retrieved data could be 
reused for a limited period. This helped reduce unnecessary API calls while allowing the data 
to be refreshed after the configured time.
